I'm not totally sure what you want but you can look in here
https://github.com/hadley/scales/tree/master/R

for discrete color scales, ie a discrete variable actually inside the aesthetic:

https://github.com/hadley/scales/raw/master/R/pal-hue.r

## source the above function, though R seems unable to source an https
## so cut and paste will probably have to work

## you get the colors which can then be used in ggplots scale_manual() via:
hue_pal()(5)

## easy way to look at the colors
## install.packages("gridExtra")
library(gridExtra)
grid.colorstrip(hue_pal()(5))
grid.colorstrip(hue_pal()(5)[c(1, 3, 5)])

